# Browser caching for the static assets the public Worker serves from `dist/web`.
#
# The SPA bundle is fingerprinted (Vite puts a content hash in the file name), so
# a given URL never changes content and can be cached indefinitely. The public
# Worker deliberately does not rewrite the cache headers of these responses (it
# only marks HTML documents, API responses, and errors `no-store`; see
# `isPrivateResponse` in worker/index.ts), so what this file sets is what the
# browser sees.
#
# The i18n dictionaries are deliberately not listed. A Worker-rendered document
# already carries the default locale's dictionary in the bootstrap island, so the
# client fetches `/i18n/*.json` only as a fallback (a statically served shell, a
# direct request). Leaving them to the asset layer default means such a fetch is
# revalidated instead of serving a dictionary that a deploy has already replaced.
#
# Sent by the asset layer for every environment, including local development.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31556952, immutable
